<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia Oct housing finance down 5.8 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia Oct housing finance down 5.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance commitments for owner-occupied housing in Australia fell 5.8 percent by volume to 40,049 dwellings in October, seasonally-adjusted, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In value terms, housing finance fell to A$3.97 billion in October from A$4.14 billion in September, the bureau said.  </p>
<p>Australian housing finance, October 1996 -</p>
<p>    Dwelling commitments	Oct 96    Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p>    Seasonally-adjusted	 40,049     42,536     39,070</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		    40,886     40,910     37,797</p>
<p>    Trend			   41,317     40,640     38,025</p>
<p>Value (A$ billion)</p>
<p>    Seasonally-adjusted	  3.97	 4.14	  3.72</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		     4.06	 4.04	  3.61</p>
<p>    Trend estimates		4.08	 4.01	  3.65</p>
</text>
